  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data above 298 K estimated except temperature of fusion. \nPhase change: 1363 K, melting point of SiS₂; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.07$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td>298.15-1363 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 12.746 + 6.608x $10^{-3}$ T + 0.012x $10^5$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"3\">1363-1600 K:</td><td> $H^o-H_2^o_{98}$  = 12.746x $10^{-3}$ T + 3.304x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  - 0.012x $10^2$ T $^{-1}$  - 4.090</td></tr><tr><td> $Cp^o$  = 23.900</td></tr><tr><td> $H^o-H_2^o_{98}$  = 23.900x $10^{-3}$ T - 9.086</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-1363 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -98.600 - 1.276 \\times 10^{-3} T + 2.633 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} - 168.000 T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -98.600 + 1.276 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T - 2.633 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} - 84.000 T^{-1} + 32.715 \\times 10^{63} T$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">1363-1600 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -103.596 + 9.878 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.671 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} - 166.800 T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -103.596 - 9.878 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T + 0.671 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} - 83.400 T^{-1} + 112.380 \\times 10^{-3} T$ </td></tr></table>\nSource: Data from Gurvich (49) who estimated all above 298 K except temperature of fusion. ",
